  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.1.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.1.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "A certain person inveighs against generation, calling it corruptible and destructive; and some one does violence [to Scripture], applying to pro-creation the Saviour’s words, “Lay not up treasure on earth, where moth and rust corrupt;”",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.1.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.1.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and he is not ashamed to add to these the words of the prophet: “You all shall grow old as a garment, and the moth shall devour you.”",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And, in like manner, they adduce the saying concerning the resurrection of the dead, “The sons of that world neither marry nor are given in marriage.”—Clem. Alex.: iii. c. 12, § 86.",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.3.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.3.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Tatian, who maintaining the imaginary flesh of Christ, pronounces all sexual connection impure, who was also the very violent heresiarch of the Encratites, employs an argument of this sort:",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.3.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.3.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "“If any one sows to the flesh, of the flesh he shall reap corruption;” but he sows to the flesh who is joined to a woman;",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.3.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.3.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "therefore he who takes a wife and sows in the flesh, of the flesh he shall reap corruption.—Hieron.: Com. in Ep. ad Gal.",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.4.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.4.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Seceding from the Church, and being elated and puffed up by a conceit of his teacher, as if he were superior to the rest, he formed his own peculiar type of doctrine.",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.4.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.4.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Imagining certain invisible Æons like those of Valentinus, and denouncing marriage as defilement and fornication in the same way as Marcion and Saturninus,",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.4.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.4.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and denying the salvation of Adam as an opinion of his own.—Irenæus: Adv. Hœr., i. 28.",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Tatian attempting from time to time to make use of Paul’s language, that in Adam all die, but ignoring that “where sin abounded, grace has much more abounded.”—Irenæus: Adv. Heres., iii. 37.",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.6.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.6.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Against Tatian, who says that the words, “Let there be light,” are to be taken as a prayer.",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.6.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.6.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If He who uttered it knew a superior God, how is it that He says, “I am God, and there is none beside me”?",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.7.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.7.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "He said that there are punishments for blasphemies, foolish talking, and licentious words, which are punished and chastised by the Logos.",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.7.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.7.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And he said that women were punished on account of their hair and ornaments by a power placed over those things, which also gave strength to Samson by his hair,",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.7.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.7.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and punishes those who by the ornament of their hair are urged on to fornication.—Clem. Alex.: Frag.",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.8.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.8.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But Tatian, not understanding that the expression “Let there be” is not always precative but sometimes imperative, most impiously imagined concerning God, who said “Let there be light,”",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.8.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.8.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "that He prayed rather than commanded light to be, as if, as he impiously thought, God was in darkness.—Origen: De Orat.",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.9.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.9.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Tatian separates the old man and the new, but not, as we say, understanding the old man to be the law, and the new man to be the Gospel.",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.9.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.9.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "We agree with him in saying the same thing, but not in the sense he wishes, abrogating the law as if it belonged to another God.—Clem. Alex.: Strom., iii. 12.",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.10",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Tatian condemns and rejects not only marriage, but also meats which God has created for use.—Hieron.: Adv. Jovin., i. 3.",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
      160,
      180
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments#Tat.Frag.11.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/tatian-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Tat.Frag.11.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "“But ye gave the Nazarites wine to drink, and commanded the prophets, saying, Prophesy not.”",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 170,
    "date_range": [
